WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.402
Lesson two point seven.

2
00:00:01.754 --> 00:00:04.281
How XMIDI's songs were split into training

3
00:00:04.281 --> 00:00:06.867
and validation, with no song IDs to go on.

4
00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:13.547
Every split here follows one rule: all the

5
00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:15.624
copies of a song go to the same side.

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.149
Lesson two point four showed why:

7
00:00:18.149 --> 00:00:20.506
otherwise the model is scored on songs it

8
00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:21.517
has already heard.

9
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.138
Lakh's split knows which files are the

10
00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:26.197
same song from two outside sources:

11
00:00:26.197 --> 00:00:27.954
Raffel's match to the Million Song

12
00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:30.163
Dataset, which gives recording IDs, and

13
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.372
the web paths each file was scraped from,

14
00:00:32.372 --> 00:00:34.180
which often read artist slash title.

15
00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:36.037
An XMIDI file has none of that.

16
00:00:36.339 --> 00:00:38.498
Its name holds an emotion, a genre and a

17
00:00:38.498 --> 00:00:39.000
random ID.

18
00:00:39.301 --> 00:00:41.209
No artist, no title, no recording.

19
00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.946
On Lakh, the melody fingerprint was the

20
00:00:43.946 --> 00:00:46.239
check: it measured how many same-song

21
00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:47.465
pairs the split missed.

22
00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:50.130
On XMIDI it's the only relation there is,

23
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.783
so it becomes the split itself.

24
00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:54.661
Keep that in mind; chapter five comes back

25
00:00:54.661 --> 00:00:55.567
to what it costs.

26
00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:00.939
Every one of the forty thousand six

27
00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:03.197
hundred and ninety-four songs is sketched

28
00:01:03.197 --> 00:01:05.240
with the fingerprint from lessons two

29
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.799
point four and two point six.

30
00:01:07.122 --> 00:01:09.434
Two songs are twins if they share at least

31
00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.692
thirty-two hashes, with a Jaccard of at

32
00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:12.391
least a half.

33
00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:13.872
Picture six songs.

34
00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.770
A and B are twins, B and C are twins, and

35
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:17.773
E and F are twins.

36
00:01:18.108 --> 00:01:20.114
A and C are not twins of each other.

37
00:01:20.621 --> 00:01:23.013
Union-find joins every linked pair into

38
00:01:23.013 --> 00:01:26.062
one group, and follows chains: A, B and C

39
00:01:26.062 --> 00:01:28.573
become one cluster, because A reaches C

40
00:01:28.573 --> 00:01:29.170
through B.

41
00:01:29.529 --> 00:01:31.980
D, with no twin, is a cluster of one.

42
00:01:32.339 --> 00:01:34.073
E and F are a cluster of two.

43
00:01:35.576 --> 00:01:37.913
In the code: for each song, the later

44
00:01:37.913 --> 00:01:40.198
songs sharing at least thirty-two hashes,

45
00:01:40.198 --> 00:01:42.275
their Jaccard, and if it's at least a

46
00:01:42.275 --> 00:01:43.002
half, union.

47
00:01:43.313 --> 00:01:45.650
Every pair that passes is joined, not only

48
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:46.844
each song's best match.

49
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.599
On the real corpus: thirteen thousand four

50
00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:51.446
hundred and fifty-one twin pairs make

51
00:01:51.446 --> 00:01:53.390
thirty-three thousand three hundred and

52
00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.070
nine clusters.

53
00:01:54.362 --> 00:01:56.597
Twenty-eight thousand songs stand alone;

54
00:01:56.597 --> 00:01:58.881
the other twelve thousand, thirty percent,

55
00:01:58.881 --> 00:02:00.387
sit in clusters of two or more.

56
00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:03.060
Most of those are pairs, and one is huge:

57
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.615
two hundred and forty-two songs.

58
00:02:05.995 --> 00:02:08.083
That giant is a chain, like A, B, C, but

59
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.404
two hundred and forty-two long.

60
00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.535
It mixes every genre: ninety-three pop

61
00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:13.367
songs, fifty-five country, fifty-three

62
00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.092
rock, and more.

63
00:02:14.347 --> 00:02:15.881
It's six tenths of a percent of the

64
00:02:15.881 --> 00:02:17.671
corpus, under the one percent rule that

65
00:02:17.671 --> 00:02:19.376
would send it to training automatically.

66
00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:21.549
It landed in training anyway, by the order

67
00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:22.657
the next chapter explains.

68
00:02:22.913 --> 00:02:24.490
Lakh's biggest chain was about seven

69
00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.129
thousand files.

70
00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.660
First the clusters are put in a fixed

71
00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.901
order: by a hash of each cluster's

72
00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:33.630
smallest md5.

73
00:02:33.966 --> 00:02:36.432
That order is as good as random, but it's

74
00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:38.953
the same every time, so anyone can rebuild

75
00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:39.514
the split.

76
00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:42.362
Then, one cluster at a time: give it to

77
00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.230
the side that is furthest behind its

78
00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:44.533
share.

79
00:02:44.836 --> 00:02:47.007
n k is the songs that side has so far, N

80
00:02:47.007 --> 00:02:48.925
is all forty thousand six hundred and

81
00:02:48.925 --> 00:02:51.349
ninety-four, and t k is its target: nine

82
00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:53.419
tenths for train, a twentieth each for

83
00:02:53.419 --> 00:02:54.428
validation and test.

84
00:02:54.731 --> 00:02:56.599
Arg min picks the side with the most

85
00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:57.256
negative gap.

86
00:02:57.749 --> 00:03:00.047
At the start every side has nothing:

87
00:03:00.047 --> 00:03:02.235
train's gap is minus nine tenths, the

88
00:03:02.235 --> 00:03:04.696
others minus one twentieth, so train takes

89
00:03:04.696 --> 00:03:05.681
the first cluster.

90
00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:07.970
Here is each side filling toward its own

91
00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:08.279
target.

92
00:03:08.725 --> 00:03:11.068
Train is so far behind that it takes every

93
00:03:11.068 --> 00:03:13.412
cluster until it holds eighty-five percent

94
00:03:13.412 --> 00:03:15.701
of the songs: the first twenty-eight

95
00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.717
thousand two hundred and fifty-eight

96
00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:18.208
clusters.

97
00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.062
From then on the three sides take turns,

98
00:03:21.062 --> 00:03:23.516
and each ends at its share: thirty-six

99
00:03:23.516 --> 00:03:25.913
thousand six hundred and twenty-five songs

100
00:03:25.913 --> 00:03:28.366
in train, two thousand and thirty-four in

101
00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:30.764
validation, two thousand and thirty-five

102
00:03:30.764 --> 00:03:31.210
in test.

103
00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:32.483
Why this shape?

104
00:03:32.813 --> 00:03:35.289
Clusters can't be cut in half, so an exact

105
00:03:35.289 --> 00:03:37.325
ninety, five, five is impossible.

106
00:03:37.655 --> 00:03:39.690
Giving each cluster to the side most

107
00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.891
behind keeps every side as close to its

108
00:03:41.891 --> 00:03:42.936
share as it can be.

109
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.412
Validation ends with seventeen hundred

110
00:03:45.412 --> 00:03:47.448
clusters, the largest eleven songs.

111
00:03:50.907 --> 00:03:53.210
After the split, each validation song is

112
00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.513
checked against the whole training side,

113
00:03:55.513 --> 00:03:56.906
with the same fingerprint.

114
00:03:57.228 --> 00:03:59.638
Twins at the rule: zero of two thousand

115
00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:00.495
and thirty-four.

116
00:04:00.985 --> 00:04:03.228
That zero is guaranteed, not discovered.

117
00:04:03.548 --> 00:04:05.898
If a validation song had a training twin,

118
00:04:05.898 --> 00:04:08.035
the two would have been joined into one

119
00:04:08.035 --> 00:04:10.064
cluster, and dealt to the same side.

120
00:04:10.502 --> 00:04:12.294
Below the rule, overlap remains.

121
00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.718
Four hundred and sixty-seven validation

122
00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:16.773
songs, twenty-three percent, share

123
00:04:16.773 --> 00:04:18.670
thirty-two hashes or more with some

124
00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.936
training song, at a Jaccard under a half.

125
00:04:21.252 --> 00:04:23.307
On Lakh the same figure is twenty-five

126
00:04:23.307 --> 00:04:23.729
percent.

127
00:04:24.045 --> 00:04:26.311
Whether those are the same songs, nobody

128
00:04:26.311 --> 00:04:26.996
has measured.

129
00:04:27.461 --> 00:04:29.750
And for scale, a simulation on the real

130
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.367
clusters: splitting song by song at random

131
00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.548
instead would have left twenty-seven to

132
00:04:34.548 --> 00:04:36.729
twenty-nine percent of validation songs

133
00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:38.474
with a cluster-mate in training.

134
00:04:41.993 --> 00:04:44.024
How much does this fingerprint catch?

135
00:04:44.353 --> 00:04:46.932
On Lakh, where song identity is known, the

136
00:04:46.932 --> 00:04:49.181
same recipe was tested on pairs known to

137
00:04:49.181 --> 00:04:50.114
be the same song.

138
00:04:50.443 --> 00:04:52.474
At thirty-two shared hashes it found

139
00:04:52.474 --> 00:04:54.394
fourteen point six percent of them.

140
00:04:54.859 --> 00:04:57.075
Picture seven pairs that really are the

141
00:04:57.075 --> 00:04:57.629
same song.

142
00:04:57.962 --> 00:05:00.178
The fingerprint joins about one of them.

143
00:05:00.511 --> 00:05:02.672
The twin rule adds the Jaccard test on

144
00:05:02.672 --> 00:05:04.556
top, so it can only catch fewer.

145
00:05:05.195 --> 00:05:07.524
It sees only the guitar's top line, so it

146
00:05:07.524 --> 00:05:09.535
misses the same song with a different

147
00:05:09.535 --> 00:05:11.917
guitar part, a different arrangement, or

148
00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:13.558
the tune on another instrument.

149
00:05:14.016 --> 00:05:15.251
So compare the two honestly.

150
00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.147
Lakh was split by metadata, so the

151
00:05:17.147 --> 00:05:19.131
fingerprint is still an independent check,

152
00:05:19.131 --> 00:05:20.895
and it finds eight point one percent of

153
00:05:20.895 --> 00:05:22.923
